    <string name="prop_sec_about">ABOUT THESE VALUES</string>
    <string name="prop_about_text">Values come from %1$s. A value shown as NO DATA was not available or could not be read; the app never estimates it. Higher solar flux generally helps the higher HF bands (15 m and up). A K-index of 5 or more means a geomagnetic storm, which often degrades HF and polar paths. These are general indicators, not a forecast for a specific path.</string>
    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_card_title">CHORNOBYL HAMDASH 0.1.0</string>
    <string name="about_text">A dashboard for licensed radio amateurs working in the Chornobyl region: public repeater information, DMR parameters, band and digital mode references, UTC and local clocks, and basic propagation data. It is not a navigator and is not intended for any military purpose.</string>
    <string name="about_sec_sources">DATA SOURCES</string>
    <string name="src_repeaters_title">Repeaters and talkgroups</string>
    <string name="src_repeaters_body">Bundled demo catalog shipped with the app. Its repeaters are fictional test entries and are labeled DEMO DATA. Replace it with a real public source before relying on it.</string>
    <string name="src_remote_title">Optional remote catalog</string>
    <string name="src_remote_body">Any https JSON catalog you enter under Settings > Data source. Entries without a stated source are rejected. The app shows each entry\'s source.</string>
    <string name="src_reference_title">Band and digital mode reference</string>
    <string name="src_reference_body">Bundled general reference based on the IARU Region 1 band plan overview and the projects\' official sites. Verify against your national allocation plan.</string>
    <string name="src_propagation_title">Propagation</string>
    <string name="src_map_title">Map</string>
    <string name="src_map_body">OpenStreetMap contributors (tiles via osmdroid, cached on the device for offline use).</string>
    <string name="about_sec_privacy">PRIVACY</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_text">Your position is used only to show you on the map, to sort distances and to compute sun times. It is never uploaded or shared, and location is requested only when you tap something that needs it. The app sends no analytics. Network requests go only to the sources listed above.</string>
    <string name="about_sec_safety">SAFETY AND LEGAL</string>
    <string name="about_safety_text">For civilian amateur radio use only. The app has no function to intercept or decode private or protected communications, search for military frequencies, locate military sites, or track people. Transmit only where your license and national rules allow it.</string>
